  "title": "Plurals",
  "summary": "How to make nouns plural in English.",
  "cefrLevel": "A1",
  "prerequisites": [],
  "theory": [
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "markdown": "Most nouns add **-s** to form the plural. Nouns ending in *-s, -x, -z, -ch, -sh* add **-es**. Nouns ending in *consonant + y* change to **-ies**.\n\nIrregular plurals: *child → children, man → men, woman → women, foot → feet, mouse → mice*."
    },
    {
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Examples",
      "headers": ["Singular", "Plural"],
      "rows": [
        ["car", "cars"],
        ["box", "boxes"],
        ["baby", "babies"],
        ["child", "children"],
        ["man", "men"]
      ]
    }
  ],
